// Teaching pseudocode, not exact Java decompiler output.
Object fetchUserAndShow(Continuation<? super Unit> completion) {
    StateMachine sm = obtainOrReuseState(completion);
    Object value = sm.result;
    switch (sm.label) {
        case 0:
            throwIfFailure(value);
            System.out.println("Start");
            sm.label = 1;
            value = api.fetchUser(sm);
            if (value == COROUTINE_SUSPENDED) {
                return COROUTINE_SUSPENDED;
            }
            // Immediate completion falls through with its value.
        case 1:
            throwIfFailure(value);
            User user = (User) value;
            System.out.println("Name: " + user.name);
            return Unit.INSTANCE;
        default:
            throw invalidResumeState();
    }
}
```

To make execution policy replaceable, **inject** the `CoroutineDispatcher` through the constructor rather than hard-coding `Dispatchers.IO`, so tests can provide a shared `TestDispatcher`. The concise repository above still uses the hard-coded form; the injected version below completes that change.

```kotlin
class MainSafeUserRepository(
    private val api: BlockingUserApi,
    private val ioDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher
) {
    suspend fun getUsers(): List<User> = withContext(ioDispatcher) {
        api.getUsers()
    }
}
```

