Non-suspending release usually needs only `finally` or `use`. Protect only necessary suspending cleanup, and keep it bounded; for cooperative cleanup you can use a small `withTimeout` inside the `NonCancellable` block. Handle cleanup failures deliberately, because they can replace the original failure. A deadline still cannot forcibly stop an uncooperative blocking API.

